BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Corning Farmers Market
DTSTART:20260924T140000Z
DTEND:20260924T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260924T141115Z
UID:1a3384f597b568a449ca9ddd74aa92b66fd46707@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Farmers Market,Community,Food,Crafts,New to the Area,Family Fun
DESCRIPTION:Corning Farmers Market\nFresh\, local\, and better than ever
 —the Corning Farmers Market is back and expanding for the season!\nJoin 
 us in downtown Corning each week to shop a wide variety of local produce\,
  baked goods\, handmade items\, and more from your favorite vendors. This 
 year\, we’re growing the market experience with additional vendors and f
 ood trucks around the Clock Tower\, bringing even more flavor\, variety\, 
 and energy to Market Street!\nThursdays\, June 4th through October 29th\n1
 0:00 AM – 2:00 PM\nDowntown Corning (Riverfront Centennial Park)\nMore w
 ays to shop:\nCustomers can use eWIC and SNAP benefits\, and we’re excit
 ed to offer Double Up Food Bucks (DUFBNY) again this year—helping you ge
 t even more fresh\, healthy food while supporting local vendors! (Some lim
 itations may apply)\nCome stroll\, shop\, and support local while enjoying
  the vibrant atmosphere of downtown Corning. There’s something for every
 one at the Farmers Market!\nImportant Update:\nWith the market expansion\,
  the Tioga Ave entrance side of the parking garage will be closed on Thurs
 days to accommodate vendors and ensure a safe\, enjoyable experience for a
 ll attendees. Please plan accordingly when visiting the market.\nA huge th
 ank you to our Summer in Downtown sponsor Williams Toyota!\n\nSource: Corn
 ing Area Chamber of Commerce - https://www.corningny.com/events/details/co
 rning-farmers-market-09-24-2026-19776
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.corningny.com/events/details/corning-farmers-market-09-24-
 2026-19776
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Guest Artist | Ruth Tamura @ CMoG
DTSTART:20260924T140000Z
DTEND:20260924T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260924T141115Z
UID:5ef1ad3dec6b00e20e154d5e581e143a147d5382@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Glass
DESCRIPTION:Guest Artist | Ruth Tamura\nSeptember 21 – 25\, 2026 10:00 a
 m–4:00 pm EDT\nAmphitheater Hot Shop\nAs part of the continued celebrati
 on of women artists of the Studio Glass Movement coinciding with the exhib
 ition Tough Stuff: Women in the American Glass Studio\, Guest Artist Ruth 
 Tamura will work with CMoG’s Hot Glass Team\, collaborating on new proje
 cts during public demonstrations of glassblowing in the Amphitheater Hot S
 hop.\nAbout the Exhibition\nTamura's work and story are featured in the ex
 hibition Tough Stuff: Women in the American Glass Studio opening May 16\, 
 2026. Tough Stuff is the first survey exhibition of work by women artists 
 working in glass during the breakthrough decades of the American Studio Gl
 ass Movement\, the 1960s through the late 1970s. Featured in the exhibitio
 n are more than 200 objects from artists such as Claire Falkenstein\, Audr
 ey Handler\, Margie Jervis\, Susie Krasnican\, Kathleen Mulcahy\, Flo Perk
 ins\, Ginny Ruffner\, Ruth Tamura\, Toots Zynsky\, and many others.\n\nSou
 rce: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78439051/202609
 21100000
GEO:42.1498;77.0542
LOCATION:Corning Museum of Glass\, One Museum Way\, Corning\, NY\, 14830
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78439051/20260921100000
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Montour Falls Farmers Market
DTSTART:20260924T200000Z
DTEND:20260924T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260924T141115Z
UID:2ca1ef1d4dfe2e7ef343056ae0189660b7392c85@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Farmers Market,Food,Crafts,Family Fun,New to the Area
DESCRIPTION:Vendor attendance will vary and is subject to change. Please c
 heck Facebook & Instagram for the latest updates including cancellations d
 ue to inclement weather and new vendor announcements. Contact vendors dire
 ctly for product availability.\nThe Montour Falls Farmers Market\, in coor
 dination with the Village of Montour Falls and the Montour Falls Fire Depa
 rtment\, supports a close-knit community by providing a place for farmers
 \, small businesses\, artisans\, and organizations to offer their products
 \, talents\, and resources. Our goal is to provide a space to shop local\,
  socialize\, and explore our community with a sustainable approach.\nMFFM 
 began in 2016 with the mission of providing fresh\, locally sourced food t
 o Montour Falls residents and creating a place for farmers to sell their p
 roducts in Schuyler County. Upon reaching that goal\, we increased our mis
 sion to include a space for socializing\, entertainment\, and education in
  an accessible\, welcoming outdoor location. The Montour Falls Farmers Mar
 ket supports local farms and small businesses\, and encourages the use of 
 SNAP/EBT.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event
 /78366788/20260611160000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78366788/20260611160000
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LGBTQ+ Roundtable @ The Waterfront Cafe
DTSTART:20260924T200000Z
DTEND:20260924T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260924T141115Z
UID:348b8ea164630d38b763bdef5d3b5677546de3ad@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Community,LGBTQ+,Connection
DESCRIPTION:Event by Tompkins Chamber\nWaterfront Cafe Ithaca\nDuration: 1
  hr 30 min\nPublic\nLooking for a supportive space to share ideas\, get ad
 vice\, and connect with mentors? The LGBTQ+ Roundtable is the perfect plat
 form for queer professionals to cultivate relationships\, explore topics r
 elevant to their professional journeys\, and advocate for LGBTQ+ represent
 ation in Tompkins County.\nRegister here: https://business.tompkinschamber
 .org/.../lgbtq-roundtable...\nThis month we are excited to meet at The Wat
 erfront Cafe! Nestled alongside the Cayuga Inlet\, their vibrant space is 
 bathed in natural light\, providing a warm and inviting atmosphere. Locate
 d within the Cayuga Wellness Center building and adjacent to Island Health
  & Fitness\, The Waterfront Cafe\, owned by Rasa Spa\, is a welcoming have
 n where you can nourish your body\, mind\, and soul. They are dedicated to
  providing a dynamic and seasonal menu that embraces the flavors of each s
 eason and supports local farms and suppliers whenever possible.\nThank you
  to our Roundtable Series Sponsors: BorgWarner\, M&T Bank\, and Rasa Spa!
 \n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78466444
 /20260924160000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78466444/20260924160000
END:VEVENT
