DESCRIPTION:Event by South Hill Cider\n550 Sandbank Road\, Ithaca\, NY\, U
 nited States\, New York 14850\nPublic\nCap Cooke is a guitarist known for 
 his work in the Finger Lakes old-time community. He’s performed alongsid
 e Pete Thompson and others in notable events where they played fiddle tune
 s with banjo\, bass\, and guitar accompaniment Cooke’s style is rooted i
 n traditional Appalachian and old-time guitar techniques\, and he’s part
  of the vibrant local music scene that supports live\, in-person playing.
 \nIn short\, Cap Cooke and Pete Thompson are key figures in keeping old-ti
 me music alive in the Finger Lakes\, performing together and recording mus
 ic that honors the region’s rich tradition.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - htt
