BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mozart in France: Theatrical and Pictorial Contexts @ Johnson Muse
 um of Art
DTSTART:20260929T163000Z
DTEND:20260929T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260924T141115Z
UID:5487d907bc0c49ab629dfba18ef17de3631aacb3@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art
DESCRIPTION:Robinson Lecture Hall and Lynch Conference Room\nStep back int
 o eighteenth-century Paris for an immersive afternoon of musical performan
 ce\, art\, and dance inspired by Mozart’s playful 1778 ballet-pantomime
 \, Les petits riens (The Little Nothings)\, as French artworks from the Jo
 hnson Museum bring the era’s world of theater\, flirtation\, and spectac
 le to vivid life.\nHear from Andrew C. Weislogel\, the Museum’s Seymour 
 R. Askin\, Jr. ’47 Curator\, Earlier European and American Art\; French 
 Baroque music and dance expert Rebecca Harris-Warrick\; and pianist and pi
 ano scholar Patricia Garcia Gil as they connect the visual art\, history\,
  and music of the era in the Robinson Lecture Hall on Floor 2L.\nAt 1:30PM
 \, this program will be followed by a historical dance workshop in the Lyn
 ch Conference Room on Floor 6 led by Julia Bengtsson of the New York Baroq
 ue Dance Company\, accompanied by students from the Cornell Symphony Orche
 stra. No experience is required to participate.\nCosponsored by the Cornel
 l Center for Historical Keyboards.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calend
 ar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78467659/20260929123000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78467659/20260929123000
END:VEVENT
