BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artist-in-Residence Lecture | Sula Bermudez-Silverman  @ CMoG
DTSTART:20261001T220000Z
DTEND:20261001T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260924T141115Z
UID:bb21e8945446dcaf4f4d2c69e435730d48a1ffec@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Glass
DESCRIPTION:Join us in The Studio Theater for Burke Residency recipient Su
 la Bermudez-Silverman's lecture on her practice and residency.\nBermudez-S
 ilverman is a contemporary visual artist whose subtle\, poetic works delve
  deeply into mythological and historical narratives to examine their impri
 nt. Materials such as sugar\, salt\, glass\, and resin often serve as phys
 ical homonyms\, altering motifs such as the “ball and claw” through co
 lor\, scale\, and translucency. One of four finalists for the 2025 Burke P
 rize competition by MAD\, her Burke Residency at The Studio will allow Ber
 mudez-Silverman to explore new processes and techniques that will expand h
 er use of glass as a medium.\nReservations for this event are not required
 . This lecture is free and open to the public.\nArtist presentations refle
 ct the individual artist's perspective\, practice\, and personal views\, a
 nd do not represent an official position of the Corning Museum of Glass.\n
 Presentations may occasionally touch on personal\, sensitive\, or difficul
 t subject matter.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uz
 pj/event/78466293/20261001180000
GEO:42.1498;77.0542
LOCATION:Corning Museum of Glass\, One Museum Way\, Corning\, NY\, 14830
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78466293/20261001180000
END:VEVENT
