BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Unearth a Mrual & Mari Wilson Art Opening
DTSTART:20261003T150000Z
DTEND:20261003T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260924T141115Z
UID:35db76eb1d3b63ec780d4faf7afbe8f6bc1193fa@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art,Literature
DESCRIPTION:Event by Lodi Whittier Library\n8484 S. Main St.\, Lodi\, NY\,
  United States\, New York 14860\nDuration: 3 hr\nPublic · Anyone on or of
 f Facebook\nAt this event\, help us celebrate "Unearth A Mural" and an exh
 ibit of mixed media by Mari Wilson.\n"Unearth a Mural" is the story of ove
 r 600 million years of life on Earth\, as told through mixed media collage
 . It features trilobites and sponges\, some of the first multicellular ani
 mals to live in the shallow oceans that once covered the area we now call 
 New York. It also includes threatened species that human communities in th
 e Finger Lakes have gathered to protect\, like ospreys and Lake Sturgeon.
 \nThis mural was created by Lodi artists and community members and facilit
 ated by local educator\, Lisbet Ratenborg over the summer of 2026. Support
  is from the Bernard Carl and Shirley Rosen Fund of the Community Foundati
 on of Tompkins County and funds from the Auburn Public Theater Regrants Pr
 ogram with the support of the Office of the Governor and New York State Le
 gislature and administered by the Auburn Public Theater.\nWe hope this liv
 ely depiction of biological diversity inspires you to dive further into re
 ading and exploring the geological time scale and eras of prehistoric life
  on Earth.\nMari Wilson is a multimedia artist from Trumansburg who create
 s drawings\, paintings\, prints\, clothing\, and much more. She is inspire
 d by rock and pop music\, politics\, friends and family\, and her unique e
 xperience of the world. Mari wants to help others with her art.\n\nSource:
  FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78458738/2026100311
 0000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78458738/20261003110000
END:VEVENT
