BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Louis K. Thaler Concert Violinist Series presents Curtis Stewa
 rt\, violinist and composer
DTSTART:20261007T230000Z
DTEND:20261008T035959Z
DTSTAMP:20260924T141115Z
UID:561129db7a3c7766a7e195816cd65b83489085ba@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:The Louis K. Thaler Concert Violinist Series presents Curtis S
 tewart\, violinist and composer\nWednesday\, October 7\, 2026\n7:00PM | Ho
 ckett Family Recital Hall at Ithaca College\nPraised for “combining omni
 vory and brilliance” (The New York Times )\, seven-time GRAMMY® Award-n
 ominated violinist and composer Curtis Stewart translates stories of Ameri
 can self-determination to the concert stage. Tearing down the facade of 
 “classical violinist\,” he treats his art as a catalyst for realizing 
 citizenship. Passionate about elevating the voices of others\, Stewart is 
 described by The New York Times as “gregarious and charismatic\, with an
  easygoing charm you rarely encounter in the intense\, inward-facing world
  of classical music.”\nAs a solo violinist\, composer\, Artistic Directo
 r of the American Composers Orchestra\, professor at The Juilliard School
 \, and member of the award-winning PUBLIQuartet\, Stewart finds personal a
 nd powerful connections among styles\, cultures\, and musics. He was award
 ed a 2025 Sphinx Medal of Excellence in recognition of extraordinary leade
 rs in the classical music field who are transforming lives while addressin
 g systemic obstacles within Black and Latino communities.\nStewart’s mos
 t recent project\, 24 American Caprices \, a contemporary response to the 
 virtuoso violin caprice tradition\, received its world premiere with the G
 ateways Festival Orchestra at the Eastman School of Music and Kaufman Musi
 c Center\, with future performances to include Boston University Tanglewoo
 d Institute\, D-Composed\, and 92NY. The world premiere recording was rele
 ased in summer 2026 on Bright Shiny Things\, featuring Stewart alongside v
 iolinists Tai Murray\, Deborah Buck\, Melissa White\, Njioma Grevious\, Ru
 bén Rengel\, and students from The Juilliard School\, Special Music Schoo
 l\, and the Perlman Music Program. The caprices are quickly being adopted 
 into the canon\, including as audition pieces for prestigious conservatori
 es such as The Juilliard School and Yale School of Music. Read the profile
  in The New York Times .\nAdditional highlights of Stewart’s 2026-2027 s
 eason include his appointment as Artist-in-Residence with the Wyoming Symp
 hony\; the world premiere of a Bartók recomposition with the Northwest Si
 nfonietta led by Jeff Meyer\; the premiere of a new commission from Nova L
 inea Music\; a solo cello work premiered by Amy Barston at The Juilliard S
 chool\; and a performance of Barber's Violin Concerto with the Anchorage S
 ymphony.\nReserve your FREE tickets here:\nhttps://www.purplepass.com/even
 ts/386747-louis-k-thaler-concert-violinist-series-oct-7th-2026\n\nSource: 
 FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78473726/20261007190
 000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78473726/20261007190000
END:VEVENT
