BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Greater Ithaca Art Trail - Open Studio Weekends!
DTSTART:20261011T150000Z
DTEND:20261011T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260924T141115Z
UID:7d931909d0bed47afb70f72f61502042501d5869@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art
DESCRIPTION:Event by Community Arts Partnership of Tompkins County\nTompki
 ns County\nDuration: 9 days\nPublic\nThe Greater Ithaca Art Trail\, a prog
 ram of the Community Arts Partnership of Tompkins County\, is a year-round
  guide to 55 fine & functional artists.\nOn October 10-11 and 17-18\, from
  11:00am to 5:00pm each day\, OVER 35 OF THOSE ARTISTS OPEN THEIR STUDIO t
 o you!\nVisitors can gather their art loving family and friends and enjoy 
 a drive through beautiful October fall foliage with artist studios as dest
 inations.\nThere’s no fee and no appointments needed. Just a wonderful f
 all adventure with great art to see or buy\, and great conversations.\nYou
 ’ll meet painters\, illustrators\, photographers\, sculptors\, multi-med
 ia artists\, printmakers\, and potters. You’ll see wood turning\, wood c
 arving\, calligraphy\, gourd art\, fine jewelry\, kiln-formed glass\, and 
 more.\nThe artists will be thrilled to share their passion for their art m
 aking and show off what they’ve been working on!\nA visitor once said\, 
 “I was blown away by the quality of the art that I saw and the really co
 ol art studios. And I didn’t expect all the wonderful conversations I ha
 d with the artists. The Art Trail is\nsuch a unique and special event. And
  when you combine visiting such great artists with the beauty of the area
 \, this is definitely going to be an annual event for me and I’ll be sur
 e to bring heaps of friends each year!”\nThose who are on a quest to buy
  art will find prices ranging from $10 to $5\,000 and everything in betwee
 n. Purchasing art can be an exhilarating experience and connecting with th
 e artist is part of that experience.\nAt ArtTrail.com you’ll find the pd
 f OCTOBER OPEN STUDIO LIST/MAP on the event page\, a list of raffle items
 \, plus artist profile pages and more.\nREGISTRATION IS REQUESTED so we ca
 n keep visitors up to date on any potential changes. Those who register ar
 e entered into two great raffles with over 25 chances to win art work or d
 iscounts from participating artists\, and Downtown Ithaca and Rasa Spa gif
 t cards.\nQuestions: Robin Schwartz\, Community Arts Partnership Program D
 irector. Info@artspartner.org\nThe Community Arts Partnership thanks our A
 rt Trail business sponsors: P.W. Wood & Son\, Harris Beach Murtha Attorney
 s at Law\, Cornell University\, and our media sponsors WSKG and The Route 
 WITH Radio. Additional funding is from the Tompkins County Tourism Program
 .\nThe Art Trail is a program of the Community Arts Partnership of Tompkin
 s County. For over 33 years\, “CAP” has been a driving force behind th
 e vibrant arts community of Ithaca and Tompkins County. To learn more abou
 t CAP events\, workshops\, and grants\, visit ArtsPartner.org\n\nSource: F
 LXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78466288/202610101100
 00
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78466288/20261010110000
END:VEVENT
