DTSTART:20261029T211500Z
DTEND:20261029T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260924T141115Z
UID:e77020296a21935f2398564deb3c059084da4f9a@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art
DESCRIPTION:Robinson Lecture Hall\, Floor 2L\nAnastasia Samoylova will dis
 cuss her work\, on view in the exhibition Atlantic Coast\, in conversation
  with Molly Kalkstein\, the Gary and Ellen Davis Curator of Photography at
  the Johnson Museum.\nAtlantic Coast is a new body of work in which Samoyl
 ova traces the complexities of American identity through photographic jour
 ney from Florida to Maine\, inspired by Berenice Abbott’s 1954 project d
 ocumenting the historic US Route 1.\nAll are encouraged to visit the exhib
 ition in the Bartels Gallery on Floor 1L prior to the talk\, which will al
 so be live streamed. The exhibition will also be open after the program du
 ring a public reception\, free and open to all.\nThis program is supported
  through a generous gift from the Hinsta Family and in part by the Findlay
  Lecture Endowment.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0
 uzpj/event/78467660/20261029171500
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78467660/20261029171500
END:VEVENT
